{
  "summary": "This image-only experiment (ResNet-50, single profile, no RNA) was designed to isolate the image modality's standalone contribution by removing RNA from the multimodal config_016. The validation accuracy of 0.208 (F1 0.172) is dramatically below both the RNA-only baseline (0.485) and the multimodal configuration (0.527), indicating that the image modality provides very weak standalone predictive signal in this setup and that the ~4.2% multimodal gain over RNA-only is unlikely to be attributable to the image's independent strength. It remains uncertain whether the multimodal improvement reflects genuine cross-modal complementarity, a specific property of the concat fusion with PCA features, or some other factor, and whether the poor image-only performance stems from a ResNet-50 limitation on this imaging data, the absence of aggregation, or inherent task difficulty for the image modality alone."
}

